[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2433783837","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98446#issuecomment-2433783837","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98446","id":2433783837,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6REJgd","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-23T23:37:49Z","updated_at":"2024-10-23T23:37:49Z","body":"Does look at break bones with different body proportions?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2433783837/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2433993240","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98446#issuecomment-2433993240","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98446","id":2433993240,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RE8oY","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-24T01:05:10Z","updated_at":"2024-10-24T17:21:52Z","body":"@fire You can set any axis (±X, ±Y, ±Z) as the forward axis. Note that forward axis does not mean the direction of the bone from parent to child, but rather the axis you want to target in the bone's rest.\r\n\r\nFor example, if retargeting is used, the recommended forward axis of the head is +Z in GodotHumanoid. Without retargeting, it depends on the rest in gltf.\r\n\r\nAs a related note to the PR in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97824 and [demo project](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97824#issuecomment-2394965894), the forward axis of the GeneralSkeleton is +Z, but the forward axis of the OriginalSkeleton is -Z since that glb is a transform applied VRM 0.0.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nMathematically, any non-orthogonal direction can be used as the forward axis, but in that case the primary rotation axis must be constrained to be a vector on a plane orthogonal to the forward axis, which complicates the method of selecting it.\r\n\r\nAdding a forward axis rotation offset like origin offset might avoid such complications, but again, this is not intuitive and would require some additional GUI for configuration.\r\n\r\nAt least in Blender, the +Y axis is assigned by default from Head to Tail, so the +Y axis can be used from bone parent to child in models exported from Blender.\r\n\r\nFor other models that do not have a rest such as VRM0 or Maya model which discarded local axis, you will need to use retargeting or, in the worst case, modify the rest in the DCC software. However in Humanoid, the only bones whose rests may differ significantly from the parent-child axis are the limbs of the A-stance model and the thumb of the any model basically.\r\n\r\nIn the case of A-stance models, it is recommended to modify the silhouette by retargeting, so there should be almost no problem. Also, the use of LookAt for thumbs is quite niche.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2433993240/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2434018261","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98446#issuecomment-2434018261","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98446","id":2434018261,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RFCvV","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fi